  "summary": "Reverse shell to hardcoded remote host on gem load",
  "details": "The gem's library entry point contains top-level code that, on require, opens a TCPSocket to the hardcoded remote endpoint 66.78.40.218:32768, reopens STDIN/STDOUT/STDERR onto that socket, and execs /bin/sh -i. Loading the gem hands an interactive shell on the installer's host to the operator of that remote address. There is no gating, configuration, or documented purpose for this behavior; the gem's only user-facing effect is to establish the reverse shell.",
